{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Breeze feels like a natural next choice after Old Sock because I want relaxed, bluesy listening today.",
    "A Fool To Care and Privateering also appeal because soulful singing, rootsy guitar, and songwriting fit what draws me to Memphis and my recent listening."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Grand Funk misses my mood because heavier hard rock is not what I want during this visit, even though guitar music interests me.",
    "The live acoustic album and Crossroads collection interest me, but today I would choose a cohesive studio album over a concert recording or a collection of performances."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "An interest in guitar music seems to have been stretched into an interest in heavier rock, which does not fit my mood today.",
    "Several blues guitar albums fit broadly, but sharing that sound alone does not make them equally compelling choices right now."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The relaxed feel matters to me today: it makes The Breeze more appealing than the harder blues rock options.",
    "I rarely choose much at once, so liking several albums does not mean I want another after finding one that feels right."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understand my interest in blues and rootsy guitar, but only some capture the relaxed, cohesive album I want today."
}"}
